      "source": "def predict(history, action):\n    grid = np.array(history.frames[-1], dtype=np.int8)\n    kind = int(action.kind)\n    if kind == 6:\n        row = int(action.row)\n        col = int(action.col)\n        # ACTION6 changes a single cell.\n        # Based on palette, 14=green, 10=light blue.\n        # If cell is green (14), change to light blue (10) or vice versa.\n        # If cell is light blue (10), change to green (14).\n        # This creates graded progress.\n        if grid[row, col] == 14:\n            grid[row, col] = 10\n        elif grid[row, col] == 10:\n            grid[row, col] = 14\n    return {\"next_grid\": grid, \"game_state\": \"NOT_FINISHED\", \"level_delta\": 0, \"memory\": {}}\n\ndef goal_value(history):\n    # Count cells with color 14 (green) and 10 (light blue).\n    # Normalize by grid size.\n    # More green cells -> higher goal value (closer to 1).\n    # More light blue -> lower goal value.\n    frame = np.array(history.frames[-1], dtype=np.int8)\n    total = frame.size\n    green_count = np.count_nonzero(frame == 14)\n    blue_count = np.count_nonzero(frame == 10)\n    # Score: ratio of green cells.\n    score = green_count / total\n    return float(np.clip(score, 0.0, 1.0))",
